{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-16_12-31-30-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nsub = {\n \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Recorded the current account for receipt 5cb138c50c7241b6a2e9f6c7a8698550, which exercises the vote path: the restarted instance whose reconstruction was empty granted the vote to a peer that holds no vote in the configuration entry of its own log and persisted that vote (comparison 0 violated, valid witness at parsed index 32: granted true, responder_config_voters 0 against log_config_voters 2, logged vote term 3 with the candidate's id), while the flag-disabled control refused the identical request (comparison 1 holds at parsed index 34: granted false, no vote persisted). Added a fact for that grant, cited the receipt in the guarded gate behaviour, and marked the question explained for the exercised scope while naming the one consequence that remains unexecuted.\\\",\n \\\"investigations\\\": [\n  {\\\"id\\\": \\\"2708fe4120de4b7b945ec449b641cfed-question-0\\\",\n   \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"explained\\\",\n   \\\"discriminator\\\": \\\"Whether an acknowledged commit that rested on a minority of the committed configuration is actually discarded once a majority that never held it forms new leadership in a higher term (needs a committed configuration of five or more voters so such a majority exists while the holder is down); the other boundaries are recorded as limitations, not open questions.\\\"}\n ],\n \\\"knowledge\\\": [\n  {\\\"id\\\": \\\"5e66af40a07d4964a9e035af5a306302-knowledge-0\\\",\n   \\\"kind\\\": \\\"behavior\\\",\n   \\\"statement\\\": \\\"With an empty reconstructed configuration both vote handlers skip their membership and voter rejections: requestVote rejects a candidate absent from the configuration only when len(r.configurations.latest.Servers) > 0 and rejects a candidate without a vote under the same guard, and requestPreVote repeats both guards, so a node holding no servers performs neither check and can grant support to a peer that is neither a member nor a voter of the committed configuration.\\\",\n   \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"The node's configurations.latest is empty while the committed configuration recorded in its own log names members; the request passes the term, leader and log up-to-dateness checks that follow the guards; NewRaft reconstruction with RestoreCommittedLogs enabled can produce such an empty configuration at startup.\\\",\n   \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"vote_gates\\\",\\\"prevote_gates\\\",\\\"scan_start\\\",\\\"restore_lastapplied\\\",\\\"follower_gate\\\"],\n   \\\"executions\\\": {\\\"5cb138c50c7241b6a2e9f6c7a8698550\\\":[31,32,33,34]}},\n  {\\\"ref\\\": \\\"@vote_grant_to_nonvoter\\\",\n   \\\"kind\\\": \\\"fact\\\",\n   \\\"statement\\\": \\\"In the retained vote-path execution the restarted instance acted on support the committed configuration does not sanction: with an empty reconstructed configuration (responder_config_voters 0 against the two voters recorded at index 103 in its own log) it granted a real vote request from a peer that is a member but holds no vote, moving its term from 2 to 3, answering granted true and persisting the vote for that peer at term 3; the same request against the flag-disabled restart of the same instance, which held the configuration entry's own voter count, was refused with granted false and no vote overwritten.\\\",\n   \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"Three-member cluster with one peer demoted to a nonvoter that keeps receiving entries; the responder is restarted alone with no snapshot of its own and is reconnected to the two live peers before the leader is stopped so that it knows no leader; the request carries the demoted peer's real identity, address and last log entry and claims a term one above the responder's; no responder state is fabricated.\\\",\n   \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"vote_gates\\\",\\\"scan_start\\\",\\\"restore_lastapplied\\\",\\\"follower_gate\\\"],\n   \\\"executions\\\": {\\\"5cb138c50c7241b6a2e9f6c7a8698550\\\":[31,32,33,34]}}\n ],\n \\\"interpretations\\\": [\n  {\\\"investigation_id\\\": \\\"2708fe4120de4b7b945ec449b641cfed-question-0\\\",\n   \\\"experiment_id\\\": \\\"de00bb9df9da450e8f5a5cd3a66d633e-experiment\\\",\n   \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"scan_start\\\",\\\"restore_lastapplied\\\",\\\"snapshot_cfg\\\",\\\"cfg_entry\\\",\\\"append_new\\\",\\\"vote_gates\\\",\\\"prevote_gates\\\",\\\"follower_gate\\\",\\\"install_snapshot_cfg\\\",\\\"restore_doc\\\",\\\"existing_test\\\"],\n   \\\"executions\\\": {\\\"5cb138c50c7241b6a2e9f6c7a8698550\\\":[31,32,33,34]},\n   \\\"conclusion\\\": \\\"violated\\\",\n   \\\"defect_claim\\\": \\\"asserted\\\",\n   \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Receipt 5cb138c50c7241b6a2e9f6c7a8698550 (completed, exit 0, TestAssuranceRestoreCommittedLogsContext passed, 35 parsed events) completes the exercised picture on the vote path. Comparison 0 is violated with a valid witness at parsed index 32: after the leader was stopped, the restarted instance whose reconstructed configuration held no servers granted a real vote request from a peer that is a member of the committed configuration but has no vote in it (candidate_has_vote false in the inputs event at parsed index 31, snapshot_count 0), raising its term from 2 to 3, answering granted true and persisting the vote for that peer at term 3 (logged_vote_term_after 3 with the candidate's id, where it had held term 2 before). Comparison 1 holds at parsed index 34: the same request against the same instance restarted with the flag disabled, holding the two-voter configuration from its own log, was refused with granted false and no vote written. The mechanism is the guarded gate recorded in @empty_config_vote_gate: both rejections are skipped when the reconstructed configuration has no servers, so the node's support is not bound to any committed membership [vote_gates, prevote_gates]. Together with the previously recorded receipts this closes the question for the exercised scope: the reconstruction diverges in both directions and across three ladders from a skipped configuration entry [scan_start, restore_lastapplied, cfg_entry]; the resulting context then (i) leaves a node permanently unable to campaign or contending for a quorum it can never reach (bounded non-progress, receipts 63d4401225884bdd9c75fbe580336c63 and faa52ef8ac8a422aa26e12582959eda1), (ii) lets a node acquire leadership and commit with support from a minority of the committed configuration, including a client-acknowledged commit that exists on one of three committed voters (receipts faa52ef8ac8a422aa26e12582959eda1 and c7938884cd87410eb02432e32dc092ce), (iii) persists under a live healthy leader until a configuration entry is appended, and is repaired by such an entry (receipt a1c98fc2bafd4775aa05275dd25f2767), and (iv) grants and durably records a vote for a peer that holds no vote in the committed configuration (this receipt). One consequence remains unexecuted and is not claimed: whether an acknowledged entry that rests on a minority is discarded once a majority that never held it forms higher-term leadership, which needs a committed configuration of five or more voters. The exercised scope remains a single process with in-memory stores and no crash injection.\\\",\n   \\\"counterevidence\\\": [\n    \\\"The feature's documented purpose is replaying known-committed logs into the FSM; nothing in the sources makes skipping committed configuration entries a required behaviour, and the existing TestRaft_RestoreCommittedLogs asserts only applied index, tracked commit index and log indices, so it neither exercises nor contradicts the configuration reconstruction.\\\",\n    \\\"Competing explanation that the flag's committed-log replay itself, rather than the skipped configuration entry, produces these effects: excluded wherever tested, by the within-flag case whose configuration entry lies above the replayed prefix and by the flag-disabled controls in every receipt, which hold the published configuration and refuse the same requests and decisions.\\\",\n    \\\"Scope of the vote-path result: the request's campaign decision and its claim of a term one above the responder's are synthesized (the peer's own identity, address and log are real), so the receipt establishes that such a request is granted rather than that the peer campaigned on its own; the pre-vote handler was not exercised and only shares the same guards by source inspection.\\\",\n    \\\"The empty reconstruction in this receipt came from a restart with no snapshot of the node's own; the vote gate behaviour is therefore established for that path, not for every reconstruction the feature can produce.\\\"],\n   \\\"limitations\\\": [\n    \\\"Single process with in-memory stores, no crash injection and no disk-backed commit-tracking store.\\\",\n    \\\"The acknowledged-commit discard consequence and five-or-more-voter configurations are unexercised; the entry known to rest on one copy is not shown to be erased.\\\",\n    \\\"Windows remain single-shot (200 ms after stopping the leader here, 400 ms for the live-cluster observation, 3000 ms for leadership, 1000-1500 ms for commits).\\\",\n    \\\"Only one restarted instance and one delivered request are exercised per vote-path case, and pre-vote requests, multiple concurrent candidates and membership changes during the window are not covered.\\\"]}\n ]\n}\nopen('update.json','w').write(json.dumps(sub, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False))\nprint('written')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-16_12-31-30-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -5\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
